usable: true
topic: "inf-alloc overview"
overview (156 bytes): "inf-alloc is the allocator under infinitydb's storage engine. It hands out fixed-size slots from arenas, and each arena carves its slots from aligned pages."
component arena | Arena | type | src/arena.rs | Owns a set of pages and hands out slots from them
component page | Page | type | src/page.rs | 64 KiB of memory aligned to its size
component slot-pool | Slot pool | module | src/pool/slot.rs | Keeps freed slots for reuse
component aligned | AlignedAlloc | function | src/pool/aligned.rs | Asks the OS for aligned memory
relation arena -> page: carves slots from
relation arena -> slot-pool: returns freed slots to
relation page -> aligned: is allocated by
flow "Allocate a slot"
  step "The caller asks the arena for a slot" @ src/arena.rs:42
  step "The arena takes one from the slot pool when it has one" @ src/pool/slot.rs:18-24
  step "Otherwise it bumps the pointer in its current page" @ src/page.rs:30
flow "Free a slot"
  step "The slot goes back to the pool" @ src/pool/slot.rs:40
diagram "How inf-alloc hands out memory", 297 bytes, ids ["arena", "slot-pool", "page"]
detail arena: "The arena keeps one current page and a list of full ones.", diagram "Inside the arena"
detail slot-pool: "A LIFO free list, so a freed slot is reused while it is still in cache."
citation src/arena.rs:40-58
citation src/page.rs:30
citation src/pool/slot.rs:18-24
